    <innerclass refid="classOpenSkyhawk_1_1BoardThermal" prot="public">OpenSkyhawk::BoardThermal</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceOpenSkyhawk">OpenSkyhawk</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>PDU monitoring node — board temperature from the NTC: warn / critical / sensor fault (#216). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Fed a converted reading (0.1 °C, from PduMath::ntcTempDC) roughly every 100 ms. Thresholds use hysteresis only — board temperature moves slowly, so no persistence timers. A FaultSource: critical → OVER_TEMPERATURE, an open/shorted NTC → SENSOR_FAULT. TEMP_WARN is a telemetry flag only, not a node fault.</para>
<para>This is the PDU&apos;s real board temperature (±0.5 °C class NTC between the 12 V and 5 V pours). The MCU die temperature in HEALTH_n is a separate, uncalibrated reading.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Static lifetime only (FaultSource registry rule) — construct as a global. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="copyright"><para>GPL-2.0-only — see Firmware/LICENSE </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
